From: PortareOS <hello@portare.org>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: one runtime PM reference while plugged

Since the HPD state machine went, being plugged holds the controller on
with the runtime PM reference of the call that found the sink, and the
unplug drops one. But msm_dp_bridge_detect() takes a reference on every
call and keeps it whenever the sink is plugged, and
msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle() takes another even when detect found the sink
first. Every connector probe with a monitor attached leaked one, so
after the unplug the controller never suspended: its interrupts stayed
enabled, and once the link was torn down IDLE_PATTERN_SENT fired some
60000 times a second until the next plug, enough to stall the Nova.

Give back the extra references. A detect that loses the sink also drops
the one being plugged held, since the unplug handler then sees nothing
to drop.

Reported in review of the series as merged: "Each call to detect() when
plugged increments the PM refcount without a corresponding put"
(drm-ai-reviews, hpd-refactor v6 patch 9, 2026-05-25).
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -410,6 +410,7 @@
 static int msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(struct msm_dp_display_private *dp)
 {
 	int ret;
+	bool was_plugged;
 	struct platform_device *pdev = dp->msm_dp_display.pdev;
 
 	drm_dbg_dp(dp->drm_dev, "Before, type=%d sink_count=%d\n",
@@ -417,6 +418,7 @@
 			dp->link->sink_count);
 
 	guard(mutex)(&dp->plugged_lock);
+	was_plugged = dp->plugged;
 
 	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&pdev->dev);
 	if (ret) {
@@ -436,6 +438,13 @@
 
 	dp->plugged = true;
 
+	/*
+	 * Being plugged holds the controller on with one reference, which
+	 * the unplug drops. Detect may have taken it already.
+	 */
+	if (was_plugged)
+		pm_runtime_put_sync(&pdev->dev);
+
 	return ret;
 };
 
@@ -902,7 +911,7 @@
 	struct msm_dp_display_private *priv;
 	u8 dpcd[DP_RECEIVER_CAP_SIZE];
 	struct drm_dp_desc desc;
-	bool phy_deinit;
+	bool phy_deinit, was_plugged;
 	int ret;
 
 	dp = to_dp_bridge(bridge)->msm_dp_display;
@@ -910,6 +919,7 @@
 	priv = container_of(dp, struct msm_dp_display_private, msm_dp_display);
 
 	guard(mutex)(&priv->plugged_lock);
+	was_plugged = priv->plugged;
 	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&dp->pdev->dev);
 	if (ret) {
 		DRM_ERROR("failed to pm_runtime_resume\n");
@@ -968,6 +978,14 @@
 		pm_runtime_put_sync(&dp->pdev->dev);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Being plugged holds one reference, kept by whichever call found
+	 * the sink. Every later detect gives its own back, or the controller
+	 * never suspends again; one that lost the sink drops that one too.
+	 */
+	if (was_plugged)
+		pm_runtime_put_sync(&dp->pdev->dev);
+
 	return status;
 }
 
